From bb13c0a6ad12ebaf87f9d42a808da4d4cc3bf347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samuel <samuel.madureira23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:15:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] SPURS tasks: per-task dispatch, free slots on exit; PSO
 cache keyed by code hash

- cellSpursCreateTask: serialize slot allocation (two PPU threads create
  tasks concurrently) and pass taskset+taskid to the async SPU thread
  explicitly instead of via shared globals (task 5 ran task 6's args).
- Release the task slot (and BE taskset bits) when the task program
  returns; the 129th CreateTask used to fail with NOMEM (menu hang).
- JoinTask looks the task up by slot index.
- D3D12 FP pipeline cache keys on the ucode code hash, not fp_addr: the
  game copies each FP to a ring buffer per draw, so every draw missed
  (99% of frame time in PSO creation after the main menu).
- spu_lifted_job.h: spu_coh_forget before return (use-after-free), SPU_TASKARG.
- SPU_TASKTIME timing log; r28-r31 in guest stack dumps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
